    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d953">

                <pb facs="0839" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/4863: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad
                                Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-07T12:00:00-05:00">September 7,
                        1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>163. From Wilson. Your 135, September 6, 8 p.m. We met the Dominicans this
                    morning and received full agreement in accordance with the telegram under
                    reference.</p>
                <pb facs="0840" n="828" xml:id="pg828"/>
                <p>Your final sentence reads, “Please telegraph, clean drafts of all texts”.</p>
                <p>The documents are so lengthy for coding that you would hardly receive by
                    telegraph the full texts before Sunday night<anchor n="32" xml:id="d953-f1"/> in
                    Washington. Hence I am venturing to modify your instruction and I am sending
                    full clean texts by open air mail to reach you Monday morning. [Wilson.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
